  "notes": "Quillstack docs builder for the elemental.nvim plugin. Distinctive: build diagnostics drive the whole UI — severity counts appear in top bar, Build tab badge, per-page nav badges (red error / orange warning / blue notice), a dot in the editor gutter at line 10, and an onboarding-style setup checklist whose step 5 is 'Fix warnings'. Issue cards have a 3px colored left border by severity, uppercase tinted severity pill, monospace excerpt of the offending source, a plain-language cause, then a one-click 'Closest match' fix button, a section dropdown fallback, and footer links 'Show line N in source' / 'What is a reference?' that open a help article in the Help tab. Publish button is disabled (pale blue) with the reason printed beside it in red. Source/Split/Preview segmented control is dark-filled for active state. Three independently scrolling columns. Page tab shows title/description fields and section ids (an outline). Proposed new view-switcher value 'source-split-preview' (filed)."
